			<div class="content" id="post-content-3635752">
									

<p>Some authors say that contemporary SCP articles should have a narrative. This article is an effort to make a narrative.</p>
<p>However, the SCP feels very generic as an anomaly. If there were anything that would make it distinct from all the other AIs that are SCPs, it is not as salient as it should be. With a relatively poor start, the rest of the article feels like a slog.</p>
<p>Perhaps the idea here functions better without the constraints of the SCP format?</p>

