<p><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hShY6xZWVGE">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hShY6xZWVGE</a></p>
<p>I am digging everything you are trying to do here. I especially loved the trial bit - bureaucratic tyranny ftw!!!!</p>
<p>However, if I were to characterize the article as a whole, I'd call it half-baked. Roger and Aria's relationship kind of just happens - I didn't really care abot them mostly because I didn't feel like I had witnessed anything that gave them a bond. In addition, I don't buy an experienced Foundation operative killing her husband just because she was drunk and he cheated on her with his waifu, and much of the dialogue just doesn't read as very human/compy - especially the first interview and Aria's last couple messages. For the next iteration, if this doesn't work or you'd like to revise it, I'd advise a more thorogh proofread, too - and maybe to expand on Roger and Aria's interactions, while trimming some of the less personal segments, like the part where Dark Doctor #297 casts aspersions on the Aria's willingness to comply. Maybe their day at the beach! That was a nice image.</p>

